Bounce

A tiny canvas toy where you tap to drop balls and drag to throw them around.

Description

Bounce is a small physics playground that runs in the browser. The whole screen is one black canvas. Tap anywhere and a ball drops from that spot. Press, drag and let go, and the ball gets thrown in the direction you dragged, with a faster throw the farther you pull. A thin line shows up while you drag so you can see where it's headed.

The balls fall under gravity, bounce off all four walls, and knock into each other. Each ball has a random size and one of seven colours, and it fades out and shrinks away after about 8 seconds so the screen never fills up. There's also a cap of 30 balls at once, and when you go over it the oldest one is removed.

I built it with plain HTML, CSS and JavaScript. There are no libraries, no build step and nothing to install. It uses pointer events, so it works the same with a mouse, a finger or a stylus, and the canvas is scaled for high-DPI screens so the balls stay sharp on phones.

