Getting Started
Dependencies

Any modern browser (Chrome, Firefox, Safari, Edge)
That's it. No Node, no npm, no packages.
Installing
Download or clone the repo:



Make sure these three files stay in the same folder:
index.html
script.js
style.css

Executing program
Open index.html in your browser. Double-clicking it is enough.

Tap or click to drop a ball.

Click and drag, then release, to throw one.

If you'd rather run it from a local server:

python -m http.server 8000

Then go to http://localhost:8000.

Help

The screen is blank. That's expected at first. The canvas starts empty, so tap somewhere to drop a ball. If nothing appears after that, open the browser console (F12) and check that script.js and style.css loaded. Both need to be in the same folder as index.html.

My balls keep disappearing. This is on purpose. Each ball lasts about 7 seconds, then fades out over 1 second. You can change this with the LIFE and FADE values at the top of script.js (they're in milliseconds).

A tap throws the ball instead of dropping it. A press that moves less than 12 pixels counts as a tap. Anything more counts as a drag. If it feels too touchy, raise that number in the pointerup handler.

I want it bouncier, heavier, or crowded. These constants in script.js control the feel:

const MAX = 30;      (max balls on screen)
const GRAV = 0.35;   (gravity)
const BOUNCE = 0.84;
